A commercial bank's policy on lending against gold and silver collateral must cover the following conduct-related aspects regarding the auction process:
**(1)** the **trigger event** for auction and **timeline for serving an auction notice** to the borrower [S1(3)];
**(2)** the **mode of auction** [S1(4)];
**(3)** the **notice period** allowed to the borrower/legal heir for loan settlement before auction [S1(5)];
**(4)** the **empanelment of auctioneers** [S1(6)];
**(5)** the **reserve price** (not less than 90% of current value, or 85% after two failed auctions) [S3].

An NBFC-P2P must obtain **prior written approval from the Reserve Bank** for:
1. Any allotment of shares that takes an individual/group’s holding to **26% or more** of paid-up capital ([S3]);
2. Any change in shareholding that grants the acquirer the **right to nominate a Director** ([S3]);
3. Changes in **directors or management**, as per RBI’s Governance Directions ([S3]).

Additionally, it must comply with the **Acquisition of Shareholding or Control Directions (2025)** (paragraphs 6(1), 6(2), 8–10, and 11–13) ([S1], [S3], [S9]).
